  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Many users wonder why VRChat will sometimes start & run with incredible low fps and then they restart the game to fix it. There is an explanation for this and an easier fix.\nVoiceMeter runs in the background for them and has switched to a new audio output device, but has not \"accepted\" this device yet, although it's already outputting sound to it. In this state, the device will blink red in VoiceMeter and VRChat runs with incredibly low fps. \nVRChat will then run normally again after manually selecting this output device in VoiceMeter by simply clicking on it. While this is an easy fix, most users don't know that and VRChat is somehow the only application where this is needed. I managed to help lots of people with this already, but it would be nice if VRChat could fix this, as it is easy to replicate if you know the VoiceMeter+VRChat combination-related bug.",
